# Keeps the Docker build context (repo root — see TimeCalculation.Api/Dockerfile's own comment on
# why) to just what the image actually needs. Without this, `docker build` uploads the whole repo —
# including host bin/obj (wrong RID for the container), RobTimeUI's node_modules, and .git — before
# the Dockerfile's own COPY layers even get a chance to be selective.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/node_modules/
**/.vite/
**/dist/

.git/
.github/

# Not part of the API image.
RobTimeUI/
TimeCalculation.Api.Tests/
TimeCalculationTests/
infra/

*.md
